{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread","id":1380422,"title":"Character building, optimization, and deoptimization thread.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-11T11:08:54-07:00","id":1380422,"title":"Character building, optimization, and deoptimization thread.","content":"I want to build a stealth game protagonist night. The thing about stealth protags is that, unless they are batman, they are typically very good at sneaky but only so so at fighty. They aren't bad at fighty, but they aren't great. In exalted however, Dex governs both fighty and sneaky. I want my Night Caste to be sneaking into and out of deathlord stronghold, taking vital intelligence. Can I get away with Dex 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:36:26-07:00","id":1380434,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all &quot;my character is a super sneaky Night who is all about sneaking&quot; is one of the concepts where I'd go, yeah, Dex 5 does seem pretty fair. I mean, if they're a physical character, they get 11 dots total of physical attributes (3+8), so Str 3, Dex 5, Sta 3 seems reasonable.<br /> Unless you're Mental primary for Perception and Wits and Physical Secondary?<br /> <br /> Now, as to whether you can get away with it... I'd say it simply depends on your ST and how they stat stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:00:57-07:00","id":1380437,"title":"","content":"I'd say you should go for Dex 5, but don't take like...15 combat charms. Maybe stick with 2-3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:01:17-07:00","id":1380438,"title":"","content":"You can just take dex 5 + (combat ability of your choice) 3 and be very good at sneaky but not overwhelmingly good at fighty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:23:44-07:00","id":1380442,"title":"","content":"One thing I've rarely seen done but wondered how it might play - if you're dead set on Dex 3 - is go nuts on willpower.<br /> <br /> Gives you options. It's not an efficient way of going about it, but might be fun. Makes you make more resource decisions in-game and feel you're pushing your limits more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-11-2020, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:47:17-07:00","id":1380449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380438#post1380438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just take dex 5 + (combat ability of your choice) 3 and be very good at sneaky but not overwhelmingly good at fighty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely go with this. Maybe with like a specialty in ambushes or something. Similarly, maybe take Dodge 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> You could even, and bear with me on this because it's mind-blowingly radical, have a Night Caste who doesn't favour a combat skill. Such a mythical creature has never been seen in my lifetime, but I believe they exist as a hypothetical concept.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then you can be really good at stealth without being amazing at combat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:54:44-07:00","id":1380469,"title":"","content":"I also agree with the Dex 5 combat skill at 3 idea. (I mean I would never do it myself, 2 BP for one combat skill at 5 is super cheap for how helpfull it is when you get into combat, but if you actively dont want to be good at combat its the most reasonable way to go.)<br /> <br /> Also if you want a night who focuses on sneaking and stealing stuff over combat stealth you're probably better of with Supernal Larceny over Stealth. Mental Invisibility Technique (E2, one prerquisite charm) is close to perfect invisibility outside of combat anyway, the wast majority of stealth charms are combat focused..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-11-2020, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:46:43-07:00","id":1380497,"title":"","content":"Is this for a game? Will your character be the only one in the game? If not, will you be doing this sneaky stuff alone?<br /> <br /> If there are other characters which have a more combat-centric concept, I would think the most important thing is to make sure you're substantially worse at combat than them. If the other character has less than 5 Dex 5 main combat ability, I would suggest going 5 Dex / 2 main combat ability to start.<br /> <br /> If you're alone, no backup, that should already go some way to making combat scary. I would tend to concur with everyone going 5 Dex / 3 main combat ability but you could go a little higher if the ST is prepared to fill the Deathlord's fortress with Abyssals and large battlegroups of undead or whatever threatens you.<br /> <br /> Are there Charms that are particularly effective at fleeing combat? It might be helpful to have some of those to make a character who isn't a badass in combat but also doesn't die when they get in a big fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 04-11-2020, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T15:11:53-07:00","id":1380502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380449#post1380449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could even, and bear with me on this because it's mind-blowingly radical, have a Night Caste who doesn't favour a combat skill. Such a mythical creature has never been seen in my lifetime, but I believe they exist as a hypothetical concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly any non-dawn or non-DB character that doesn't favour at least one, sometimes more than one, combat ability is basically unheard of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T16:14:15-07:00","id":1380510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread#post1380422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to build a stealth game protagonist night. The thing about stealth protags is that, unless they are batman, they are typically very good at sneaky but only so so at fighty. They aren't bad at fighty, but they aren't great. In exalted however, Dex governs both fighty and sneaky. I want my Night Caste to be sneaking into and out of deathlord stronghold, taking vital intelligence. Can I get away with Dex 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dex is too important to Stealth to lower it, to reduce combat effectiveness I'd recommend lowering the Combat ability instead. The most drastic step you can take is not favoring your combat skill, so you don't even have an Excellency, at which point you could even have 5 in it and you still wouldn't be OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380502#post1380502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly any non-dawn or non-DB character that doesn't favour at least one, sometimes more than one, combat ability is basically unheard of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, guess my groups are weird then. My Lore Supernal went up against Alhat with 8 dice on his attack roll and no Excellency, and in another game I ST the Zenith has 0 combat skills and 1 DV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 04-11-2020, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T17:01:49-07:00","id":1380517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380510#post1380510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, guess my groups are weird then. My Lore Supernal went up against Alhat with 8 dice on his attack roll and no Excellency, and in another game I ST the Zenith has 0 combat skills and 1 DV.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that my games are weird but previously everyone basically took it as a given to take a 5 in a combat ability, and if it was Thrown or Archery or something a 5 in at least Dodge as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:48:58-07:00","id":1380536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380517#post1380517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be that my games are weird but previously everyone basically took it as a given to take a 5 in a combat ability, and if it was Thrown or Archery or something a 5 in at least Dodge as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they just didn't want an unlucky decisive to splat the character they had spent three hours on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:49:20-07:00","id":1380537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380517#post1380517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be that my games are weird but previously everyone basically took it as a given to take a 5 in a combat ability, and if it was Thrown or Archery or something a 5 in at least Dodge as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... aren't your playgroup survivors of 2e? That might explain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:25:21-07:00","id":1380547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380536#post1380536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they just didn't want an unlucky decisive to splat the character they had spent three hours on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but in 3e you've got to be pretty unlucky. If you take two ox bodies and have 1-2 stamina, a 15i decisive attack has a less than 1% chance of killing you. You have to build all the way up to a 28i decisive attack to do it even half the time. It would also have to do it by a factor of 5 health levels to stop you from negating that with a crippling wound. <i>Even then</i>, incapacitation isn't 100% fatal. At ST discretion a character with his incap level filled with lethal can linger around for a few rounds, time enough to allow other characters to stabilize them.<br /> <br /> At some point you just need to accept that you messed up, or your ST was being unfair, or somehow a one in a million chance happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:54:17-07:00","id":1380557,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the first PC death to happen on my watch in 3e wasn't because of an unlucky decisive - the PC in question had been behaving so monstrously to the crew that, when he bragged about how easily he could slaughter them all and then ventured out in a lifeboat while the rest of the circle was away, the crew shot a hole in the bottom of the lifeboat with the ship's ballista and sank it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-11-2020, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T20:43:20-07:00","id":1380568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380547#post1380547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but in 3e you've got to be pretty unlucky. If you take two ox bodies and have 1-2 stamina, a 15i decisive attack has a less than 1% chance of killing you. You have to build all the way up to a 28i decisive attack to do it even half the time. It would also have to do it by a factor of 5 health levels to stop you from negating that with a crippling wound. <i>Even then</i>, incapacitation isn't 100% fatal. At ST discretion a character with his incap level filled with lethal can linger around for a few rounds, time enough to allow other characters to stabilize them.<br /> <br /> At some point you just need to accept that you messed up, or your ST was being unfair, or somehow a one in a million chance happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this is completely true for a one hit decisive. But imagine your combat unready scholar is in combat with say... a Size 2 Elite Troop Battlegroup commanded by a competent commander(something that Creation is lousy with, considering how large it is, and how many empires there are), Round 1, sure you can probably just get crashed. Round 2 onwards...? If you aren't parrying or dodging real good, then you are getting pretty close to dying. Round 3 ends the heroic epic of your character (depending on how many arms or legs you've got left to lose, of course).<br /> <br /> Most people playing Exalted don't want to see their character end potentially first session from some unlucky rolls, and becoming a combat badass in one ability is a minimal investment for Solars (and being Creation's Dexiest crafter is trivial for Lunars) so, why not?<br /> <br /> And taking two ox-bodies while possible, is not a common choice at character creation I notice (don't all of you come out of the woodwork now and say &quot;but my character...&quot; I just mean in aggregate from what I've seen online). One is like 50% of builds at least, sure, but 2 ox bodies starts to become a significant investment (almost like taking 5 dodge at character creation, say...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-11-2020, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T22:41:59-07:00","id":1380586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380568#post1380568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, this is completely true for a one hit decisive. But imagine your combat unready scholar is in combat with say... a Size 2 Elite Troop Battlegroup commanded by a competent commander(something that Creation is lousy with, considering how large it is, and how many empires there are), Round 1, sure you can probably just get crashed. Round 2 onwards...? If you aren't parrying or dodging real good, then you are getting pretty close to dying. Round 3 ends the heroic epic of your character (depending on how many arms or legs you've got left to lose, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>What size 2 battlegroup of mortals is holding up til the end of round 3 against a circle of Solars? Even if you've got just one Dawn who's not very optimized, and like, a Zenith or a Night or something who's not bad for Essence one that battlegroup is unlikely to survive until even the end of round 1. Definitely not past the end of round 2 with all of them beating on them. With an optimized Dawn they will 100% not survive to act in the first round unless he doesn't feel like spending motes/willpower.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about what if a high essence Infernal takes to the field with a Size 5 battlegroup of bloodapes, that's different. That's more a problem to do with AoE attacks, and character placement though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T00:44:30-07:00","id":1380594,"title":"","content":"Okay. Dex 5/Melee 1 it is. I'll get by with Call the Blade and an excellency.<br /> <br /> The next question in the de-optimization process. Can I afford to cut some stealth charms? I have Stalking Wolf Attitude (Blinding Battle Feint is pre-req) and Fivefold-Shadow Burial (eighth charm in it's tree). And that is a lot of charms that I could be using for her favored abilities to round out her character instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T02:06:17-07:00","id":1380604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380568#post1380568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But imagine your combat unready scholar is in combat with say... a Size 2 <b>Elite </b>Troop Battlegroup commanded by a competent commander<b>(something that Creation is lousy with, considering how large it is, and how many empires there are)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You and I seem to have differing opinions on what &quot;Creation is lousy with.&quot; if you feel like it's fairly normal for a Solar to run into a commander leading <i>several dozen</i> soldiers either handpicked for their skill and valor, or outright raised from birth training in the art of killing. These guys are the Michael Jordan of stabbing someone with a sword, and absent some potent magic, most of the places in Creation will fall short of being able to put together such a war-band trivially.<br /> <br /> \u200bTry using Battle-Ready Troops instead, perhaps, and see if that helps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-12-2020, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T03:56:33-07:00","id":1380612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380604#post1380604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and I seem to have differing opinions on what &quot;Creation is lousy with.&quot; if you feel like it's fairly normal for a Solar to run into a commander leading <i>several dozen</i> soldiers either handpicked for their skill and valor, or outright raised from birth training in the art of killing. These guys are the Michael Jordan of stabbing someone with a sword, and absent some potent magic, most of the places in Creation will fall short of being able to put together such a war-band trivially.<br /> <br /> \u200bTry using <b>Battle-Ready Troops </b>instead, perhaps, and see if that helps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey-Zeus! How many Bronze Age kingdoms even had standing armies?<br /> <br /> Battle-Ready Troops are Realm Legions. For most Satrapies and independent kingdoms, Militia should be the order of the day.<br /> <br /> Battle-Ready Troops means someone mobilized a fully trained, standing army against you. If you're fighting the town guard, or a force that's been raised especially to fight you then you're fighting Militia.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that it's unrealistic to <i>ever </i>encounter Battle Ready Troops (the Corebook makes a point of saying most BRT spend most of their time farming, and Creation is full of warfare between city-states and nomads). But let's be clear here: if you're fighting BRT then you've pissed off an actual, honest-to-goodness army. These aren't &quot;the cops&quot;, this is <i>the army</i> being called in to deal with you.<br /> <br /> Which, yes, does happen in Exalted, but it doesn't just happen in a Random Encounter.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yes, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> the &quot;Elite Troops/<b>Champion</b>&quot; profile is for the likes of Hector, Theseus, Castor, Leonidas I, Saladin, Ghengis Khan, Kal Drogo. You can make a battle group of them (that's literally what the Argonauts were -- it's very <i>Exalted</i>). But it's not something that a random peasant kingdom is <i>lousy </i>with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-12-2020, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:27:31-07:00","id":1380624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380612#post1380612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Battle-Ready Troops are Realm Legions. For most Satrapies and independent kingdoms, Militia should be the order of the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the poster specified empires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380612#post1380612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These aren't &quot;the cops&quot;, this is <i>the army</i> being called in to deal with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone said these guys were the cops.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380612#post1380612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, yes, does happen in Exalted, but it doesn't just happen in a Random Encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone said these guys were a random encounter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:52:29-07:00","id":1380628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380612#post1380612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Otherwise, yes, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> the &quot;Elite Troops/<b>Champion</b>&quot; profile is for the likes of Hector, Theseus, Castor, Leonidas I, Saladin, Ghengis Khan, Kal Drogo. You can make a battle group of them (that's literally what the Argonauts were -- it's very <i>Exalted</i>). But it's not something that a random peasant kingdom is <i>lousy </i>with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is what is intended exactly. First, most of these characters are most famous for commanding other troops, and if they appeared in a game would likely be making some Command rolls, but the Elite Troops don't have a Command pool. I'm not so familiar with what abilities the first three ones had off the top of my head, but the last four deserve their own stat blocks, although you could accomplish this by taking the Elite Troops block, modifying the weapons and armor a bit, and adding additional dice pools for other actions they would have, likely in the 6 to 9 range.<br /> <br /> Second, after Elite Troops / Champion it says Elite Bodyguard. None of these characters are bodyguards. Some of them probably had bodyguards that are mostly forgotten by history. They still would have been Elite Troops. I agree that most forces in Creation won't have a standing army, but any ruler who does have the resources to form a standing army of substantial size has the resources to pick a couple top soldiers, give them special training and &quot;enchanted brocades&quot;, and make them his bodyguards.<br /> <br /> Third, &quot;shock troops&quot; and &quot;janissaries&quot;, while rare, when you find them you will usually find them in substantial groups. There were tens of thousands of janissaries at one time in the Ottoman Empire, and the point of shock troops is to get enough powerful fighters together to break up the enemy formation. Running into a battlegroup of them should be much, much less surprising then running into the Argonauts, a legend even among legends.<br /> <br /> If your characters have reason to fight an army of thousands, and decide to run / fly/ sneak around them and go straight for the leaders (an appropriate strategy for PCs in almost any game, but surely in Exalted), they shouldn't be surprised to encounter a battlegroup of Elite Troops when they arrive. They should probably be surprised if it's more than Size 1 or 2 though, sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:17:49-07:00","id":1380654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380624#post1380624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but the poster specified empires.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone said these guys were the cops.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone said these guys were a random encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true. Empires will have battle ready troops.<br /> <br /> But we're talking about not wanting to get your bookish scholar murdered. That's not going to happen unless you set out to go fight an army. You're not going to be walking down a street in Nexus then suddenly have to fight a Size 2 battlegroup of elite troops for no reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380628#post1380628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this is what is intended exactly. First, most of these characters are most famous for commanding other troops, and if they appeared in a game would likely be making some Command rolls, but the Elite Troops don't have a Command pool. I'm not so familiar with what abilities the first three ones had off the top of my head, but the last four deserve their own stat blocks, although you could accomplish this by taking the Elite Troops block, modifying the weapons and armor a bit, and adding additional dice pools for other actions they would have, likely in the 6 to 9 range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd use the 6 die Threaten pool. 3 Charisma 3 War. &quot;The QC is skilled in this area, with competence to rival well-trained mortals or the heroic prowess of the Exalted.&quot; <br /> <br /> But I'd be okay stretching a few of them upto 9.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, after Elite Troops / Champion it says Elite Bodyguard. None of these characters are bodyguards. Some of them probably had bodyguards that are mostly forgotten by history. They still would have been Elite Troops. I agree that most forces in Creation won't have a standing army, but any ruler who does have the resources to form a standing army of substantial size has the resources to pick a couple top soldiers, give them special training and &amp;quot;enchanted brocades&amp;quot;, and make them his bodyguards.<br /> <br /> Third, &amp;quot;shock troops&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;janissaries&amp;quot;, while rare, when you find them you will usually find them in substantial groups. There were tens of thousands of janissaries at one time in the Ottoman Empire, and the point of shock troops is to get enough powerful fighters together to break up the enemy formation. Running into a battlegroup of them should be much, much less surprising then running into the Argonauts, a legend even among legends.<br /> <br /> If your characters have reason to fight an army of thousands, and decide to run / fly/ sneak around them and go straight for the leaders (an appropriate strategy for PCs in almost any game, but surely in Exalted), they shouldn't be surprised to encounter a battlegroup of Elite Troops when they arrive. They should probably be surprised if it's more than Size 1 or 2 though, sure. </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. The Realm, for example, has significant numbers of Elite Troops.<br /> <br /> I disagree that Creation is &quot;lousy&quot; with such battlegroups, casually bedecked in magical armor, just waiting to pop up and kill your bookish scholar.<br /> <br /> You have to go out of your way to fight these people. That's my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:14:57-07:00","id":1380673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380654#post1380654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All true. Empires will have battle ready troops.<br /> <br /> But we're talking about not wanting to get your bookish scholar murdered. That's not going to happen unless you set out to go fight an army. You're not going to be walking down a street in Nexus then suddenly have to fight a Size 2 battlegroup of elite troops for no reason.<br /> <br /> I'd use the 6 die Threaten pool. 3 Charisma 3 War. &quot;The QC is skilled in this area, with competence to rival well-trained mortals or the heroic prowess of the Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I'd be okay stretching a few of them upto 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure (although for Genghis Khas, Leonidas, and other generals of legend, I don't think you could go below &quot;Mortals with this level of skill are rare, true masters of their art&quot; - I mean if Genghis Khan didn't have 5 War, who else alive at that time did?) <br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;what should this guy's dice pool be&quot; is a particularly hard problem for the ST, I just think, if this was intended by the writers or devs to represent those characters, they would have thrown &quot;Command: 6 dice&quot; or something in there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't disagree. The Realm, for example, has significant numbers of Elite Troops.<br /> <br /> I disagree that Creation is &quot;lousy&quot; with such battlegroups, casually bedecked in magical armor, just waiting to pop up and kill your bookish scholar.<br /> <br /> You have to go out of your way to fight these people. That's my point. </div> </div> </div>This is a good point.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of people want their scholar characters to be able to tag along when other characters decide to battle an army singlehandedly or whatever sorts of shenanigans combat-ready Exalts get up to, not say &quot;to dangerous for me, you guys go ahead&quot; and stay at home reading books. I think you and I basically agree that a 3 in the main combat stat should be sufficient to this, and maybe even lower with reasonable Dexterity, Stamina, and defensively-focused Charms. Maybe you and I will disagree when I say that it's totally understandable for players, especially those new to the game, to overestimate this, and go higher &quot;to be safe&quot;, especially when, as prototype00 said, it's such a low investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:41:23-07:00","id":1380680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380654#post1380654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not going to be walking down a street in Nexus then suddenly have to fight a Size 2 battlegroup of elite troops for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah - there's <i>specifically</i> a law against bringing an army into Nexus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380654#post1380654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to go out of your way to fight these people. That's my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>sometimes</i> they bring the fight to you. That's what the Wyld Hunt is, after all. Or sometimes the city you're in is under siege.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:14:08-07:00","id":1380689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380673#post1380673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of people want their scholar characters to be able to tag along when other characters decide to battle an army singlehandedly or whatever sorts of shenanigans combat-ready Exalts get up to, not say &quot;to dangerous for me, you guys go ahead&quot; and stay at home reading books. I think you and I basically agree that a 3 in the main combat stat should be sufficient to this, and maybe even lower with reasonable Dexterity, Stamina, and defensively-focused Charms. Maybe you and I will disagree when I say that it's totally understandable for players, especially those new to the game, to overestimate this, and go higher &quot;to be safe&quot;, especially when, as prototype00 said, it's such a low investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is such a low investment.<br /> I think one oddity is that, looking at a sheet, 3 people with Melee 5 are as good as each other; but the Twilight with one melee charm is way better than the mortal (as in, rolling almost twice as many dice due to their excellency), and the Dawn with 10 melee charms is way better than the Twilight.<br /> But looking at the sheet, they all kind of<i> feel </i>like they should be similar. Which makes it feel weird when the Twilight scholar has Melee 5, it doesn't make sense for his backstory, but actually that doesn't make him amazing at combat (well... unless he has a single Melee charm).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a lot of people want their scholar characters to be able to tag along when other characters decide to battle an army singlehandedly or whatever sorts of shenanigans combat-ready Exalts get up to, not say &quot;to dangerous for me, you guys go ahead&quot; and stay at home reading books. I think you and I basically agree that a 3 in the main combat stat should be sufficient to this, and maybe even lower with reasonable Dexterity, Stamina, and defensively-focused Charms. </div> </div> </div>I think for this, defensive charms are the key. You don't need to be able to do massive damage, just carving a bit of initiative off the enemies and putting on another onslaught penalty is fine to help out your friends. But you don't want to get killed doing it... You also don't want to be giving out lots of initiative to the enemy because of your low defence and soak.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:41:23-07:00","id":1380699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380673#post1380673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure (although for Genghis Khas, Leonidas, and other generals of legend, I don't think you could go below &amp;quot;Mortals with this level of skill are rare, true masters of their art&amp;quot; - I mean if Genghis Khan didn't have 5 War, who else alive at that time did?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Genghis Khan? Sure. Leonidas... lost and made no significant impact on the war. 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think &amp;quot;what should this guy's dice pool be&amp;quot; is a particularly hard problem for the ST, I just think, if this was intended by the writers or devs to represent those characters, they would have thrown &amp;quot;Command: 6 dice&amp;quot; or something in there. </div> </div> </div>Who IS supposed to lead troops, if not Champions? Are all armies supposed to be led by robots?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a lot of people want their scholar characters to be able to tag along when other characters decide to battle an army singlehandedly or whatever sorts of shenanigans combat-ready Exalts get up to, not say &amp;quot;to dangerous for me, you guys go ahead&amp;quot; and stay at home reading books. I think you and I basically agree that a 3 in the main combat stat should be sufficient to this, and maybe even lower with reasonable Dexterity, Stamina, and defensively-focused Charms. Maybe you and I will disagree when I say that it's totally understandable for players, especially those new to the game, to overestimate this, and go higher &amp;quot;to be safe&amp;quot;, especially when, as prototype00 said, it's such a low investment. </div> </div> </div>It's perfectly understandable if you've come from 2E, overanalysed the Corebook, or are trying to make a character without having thoroughly read the rules.<br /> <br /> Which is to say: I don't disagree with you. The 3E Corebook is a hot mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380680#post1380680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah - there's <i>specifically</i> a law against bringing an army into Nexus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True. On the flip side, Nexus is probably one of the few places where you might realistically walk right into a Size 2 Battlegroup of Elite Tiger-Warriors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, <i>sometimes</i> they bring the fight to you. That's what the Wyld Hunt is, after all. Or sometimes the city you're in is under siege. </div> </div> </div>Also true. But again it's not something that just happens out of the blue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:57:23-07:00","id":1380703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380689#post1380689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is such a low investment.<br /> I think one oddity is that, looking at a sheet, 3 people with Melee 5 are as good as each other; but the Twilight with one melee charm is way better than the mortal (as in, rolling almost twice as many dice due to their excellency), and the Dawn with 10 melee charms is way better than the Twilight.<br /> But looking at the sheet, they all kind of<i> feel </i>like they should be similar. Which makes it feel weird when the Twilight scholar has Melee 5, it doesn't make sense for his backstory, but actually that doesn't make him amazing at combat (well... unless he has a single Melee charm).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On this, what do people think, if anything, needs doing about the '5 issue'?<br /> <br /> If the rulebook included something like 'you can only have two attributes and two abilities at 5 at chargen' does anything actually change for most people's games? Maybe a sidebar saying 'this is the default setting for Creation and NPCs assume this. But this is Exalted, feel free to ignore if that suits your game?'<br /> <br /> Is that a better game (genuine question)? Do players need this much hand holding? Leaves more space for characters to grow in their secondary fields outside charms, but (a) charms are generally the most gratifying (I.e Impactful) way to grow and (b) loads of people play 'the world's greatest warrior exalts' stories - do restrictions hamper this too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-12-2020, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:34:19-07:00","id":1380713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380699#post1380699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who IS supposed to lead troops, if not Champions? Are all armies supposed to be led by robots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all social roles are supposed to be filled by quick characters directly out of the book. If the PCs get in a social encounter with a mortal human noble, should I use the statblock from the book that's the closest approximation (maybe Spymaster?)? I should probably whip up some Resolve, Guile, Social Influence dice pool, and any other values based on general guidelines instead.<br /> <br /> I would expect the commanders of a lot of armies to have combat prowess less than an elite troop, because they're often nobles or other political leaders who know how to lead the fight from the rear but not intensively trained in battle, or else experienced soldiers well past their prime. That said, a commander skilled in hand-to-hand combat wouldn't be surprising, and in a narrative-focused setting, dueling the enemy commander is good, wholesome fun, so there's certainly no harm in giving them those stats + a command pool and maybe some more social dice pools. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's perfectly understandable if you've come from 2E, overanalysed the Corebook, or are trying to make a character without having thoroughly read the rules.<br /> <br /> Which is to say: I don't disagree with you. The 3E Corebook is a hot mess. </div> </div> </div>It actually would be somewhat hard for the Corebook to include a clear explanation of this, because if they explained what you should not do to avoid making your character overly powerful in combats against standard foes, it might lead to more players doing that, because the lure of easy power is so hard to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:45:17-07:00","id":1380717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380703#post1380703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On this, what do people think, if anything, needs doing about the '5 issue'?<br /> <br /> If the rulebook included something like 'you can only have two attributes and two abilities at 5 at chargen' does anything actually change for most people's games? Maybe a sidebar saying 'this is the default setting for Creation and NPCs assume this. But this is Exalted, feel free to ignore if that suits your game?'<br /> <br /> Is that a better game (genuine question)? Do players need this much hand holding? Leaves more space for characters to grow in their secondary fields outside charms, but (a) charms are generally the most gratifying (I.e Impactful) way to grow and (b) loads of people play 'the world's greatest warrior exalts' stories - do restrictions hamper this too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to fiddle around with the rules, I'd suggest that buying an ability from 3 to 5 shouldn't be the same cost as buying it from 0-2. Or half the cost of buying a dot of an attribute.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think if you say that favoured abilties of 4 and 5 cost 2 freebies instead of 1, then people can no longer buy 7 abilities at 5. If they buy 2 or 3... well that's probably quite fitting for most Exalted characters, so it's fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:02:25-07:00","id":1380725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380703#post1380703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On this, what do people think, if anything, needs doing about the '5 issue'?<br /> <br /> If the rulebook included something like 'you can only have two attributes and two abilities at 5 at chargen' does anything actually change for most people's games? Maybe a sidebar saying 'this is the default setting for Creation and NPCs assume this. But this is Exalted, feel free to ignore if that suits your game?'<br /> <br /> Is that a better game (genuine question)? Do players need this much hand holding? Leaves more space for characters to grow in their secondary fields outside charms, but (a) charms are generally the most gratifying (I.e Impactful) way to grow and (b) loads of people play 'the world's greatest warrior exalts' stories - do restrictions hamper this too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fine.<br /> <br /> The NPC rules are clear you don't need max stats.<br /> The static difficulty rules are clear you don't need max stats.<br /> The stat descriptions very clearly denote what a stat of 5 means.<br /> You have to spend BP to get 5s in your Abilities.<br /> The example character has one 5 (Dexterity).<br /> The five pregen characters have eight Abilities at 5 between them (one of which not having any 5s).<br /> <br /> Exalted <i><u>works</u> </i>if you take eleven 5s. It just doesn't work <i>the same way </i>as if you only take one or two 5s. What kind of game you play should be decided in Session 0 -- where you should hold the players hands WAAAY more than this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-12-2020, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:14:29-07:00","id":1380733,"title":"","content":"I think for new players, it's definitely a good idea to guide them through it.<br /> <br /> For experienced players, it's definitely a good idea... to talk to them about what you're aiming for. So that might well be &quot;no more than 2 things at 5&quot; or whatever. (That does have the advantage that the players who weren't going to optimise anyway aren't really affected, as that's what they were going to do.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:45:04-07:00","id":1380741,"title":"","content":"IDK if I'd agree NPC rules make it clear max stats isn't expected for exalted characters, going by their dice caps all the NPC Shikari in the corebook are MA 5 + speciality. Even the earth immaculate seems to have Dex 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380703#post1380703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On this, what do people think, if anything, needs doing about the '5 issue'?<br /> <br /> If the rulebook included something like 'you can only have two attributes and two abilities at 5 at chargen' does anything actually change for most people's games? Maybe a sidebar saying 'this is the default setting for Creation and NPCs assume this. But this is Exalted, feel free to ignore if that suits your game?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively print it with a sidebar titled &quot;lrn 2 solar&quot; telling you to buy at least 5 abilities to 5 at chargen and that character-sheets not comming with Dex 5 pre-filled is a printing error.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I might not be entirely serious.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-12-2020, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:48:51-07:00","id":1380743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380741#post1380741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively print it with a sidebar titled &amp;quot;lrn 2 solar&amp;quot; telling you to buy at least 5 abilities to 5 at chargen and that character-sheets not comming with Dex 5 pre-filled is a printing error.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I might not be entirely serious.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>'You must have at least a 21 dice attack pool to go on this ride...'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:17:19-07:00","id":1380750,"title":"","content":"I think it might be fine to start character creation with a bit fewer points to spend on Abilities, and maybe even Merits and Charms, and let more of that develop through play. It's not like 5s in favored Abilities are hard to train, if you want them.<br /> <br /> But I agree with John and the Wizard that what's most needed is advice. Some points more detailed than &quot;talk to your group about how many 5s you want to take, and if you're not sure, aim for a low number&quot; that I might give two new players (which anyone is free to dispute if they disagree with):<br /> <br /> (1) Remember during character creation that Abilities are relatively easy to raise, in terms of XP and training time, and Attributes less so, especially in terms of training time, while many Merits can't be gotten by spending XP at all. If you're not sure what to set an Ability on, you can start it lower and raise it later.<br /> <br /> (2) It's more important to make sure characters are balanced against each other, and the ST's expectations, in terms of their main combat stats, where they'll often be facing the same threats, than noncombat stats, where they'll usually be making different rolls. That said, it's fine to make a character who plans not to participate in combat, or to participate but focus on self-defense.<br /> <br /> (3) You can make your starting character concept quite broad. Saying your character is a ninja, a pirate, or a wizard (to pick the first three things that popped into my head) would be a good starting point in a lot of games. Your character in Exalted can easily be a ninja pirate wizard from session 1. You'll have plenty of Ability points to spread around to make your character an expert in all these things, who can reach superhuman levels by spending Essence.<br /> <br /> (4) Think about things your Circle may all want to do together, such as sneak into somewhere (Stealth) or climb something (Athletics), and make sure you have a point or two at those.<br /> <br /> (5)The suggestion in the book that you may want to start with mortal characters and Exalt as Solars during play should probably be bolded and underlined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:22:07-07:00","id":1380752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380654#post1380654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree. The Realm, for example, has significant numbers of Elite Troops.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a specific point, the Realm has 5,000 thaumaturgically enhanced giant-people with elite training, that can dual-wield halberds, have superhuman resolve, and on top of that have mysterious other powers granted to them by sorcery, or alchemically fueled battle transformations.<br /> <br /> And it's not like the Realm has those guys and then a bunch of nobody peasants. They're just one of the most elite forces they have access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:44:00-07:00","id":1380756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380741#post1380741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK if I'd agree NPC rules make it clear max stats isn't expected for exalted characters, going by their dice caps all the NPC Shikari in the corebook are MA 5 + speciality. Even the earth immaculate seems to have Dex 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 495 lays out exactly what the dice expectations for NPCs are.<br /> <br /> The Earth Immaculate is an Exalt dedicated to hunting down and murdering Solars. They should be an epic challenge fit for the returning God-Kings.<br /> <br /> You want me to run Guybrush vs the Earth Immaculate in the Arena? (I'm gonna be honest, Guybrush might actually lose that one. But I still think it would be illustrative.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:05:09-07:00","id":1380763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380756#post1380756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 495 lays out exactly what the dice expectations for NPCs are.<br /> <br /> The Earth Immaculate is an Exalt dedicated to hunting down and murdering Solars. They should be an epic challenge fit for the returning God-Kings.<br /> <br /> You want me to run Guybrush vs the Earth Immaculate in the Arena? (I'm gonna be honest, Guybrush might actually lose that one. But I still think it would be illustrative.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It could be fun. Doo eet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:18:31-07:00","id":1380767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380756#post1380756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 495 lays out exactly what the dice expectations for NPCs are.<br /> <br /> The Earth Immaculate is an Exalt dedicated to hunting down and murdering Solars. They should be an epic challenge fit for the returning God-Kings.<br /> <br /> You want me to run Guybrush vs the Earth Immaculate in the Arena? (I'm gonna be honest, Guybrush might actually lose that one. But I still think it would be illustrative.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do, maybe give him the remaining Essence 1 charm from Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style (i.e. Demure Carp Feint), just to give him a little bit more interesting things to do in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T03:46:40-07:00","id":1380896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380594#post1380594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Dex 5/Melee 1 it is. I'll get by with Call the Blade and an excellency.<br /> <br /> The next question in the de-optimization process. Can I afford to cut some stealth charms? I have Stalking Wolf Attitude (Blinding Battle Feint is pre-req) and Fivefold-Shadow Burial (eighth charm in it's tree). And that is a lot of charms that I could be using for her favored abilities to round out her character instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any more details about the concept? Genuinely intrigued. If you've got loads of, say, larceny, then maybe the stealth charms don't matter so much?<br /> <br /> What are you taking instead?<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> (Yet) Another question: how do folk feel about attribute spreads overall? For example, 5/5/1 gets you to a higher power tier far more quickly after only a few sessions of experience. It personally troubles me the least if social is primary (I can envisage someone who is, say, manipulative as all hell but not memorable easily), but the most with physical, where being a muscle-bound, hand-eye god who struggles to jog is a stretch until experience kicks in.<br /> <br /> Just take athletics and resistance as well I guess...<br /> <br /> What quirks/favoured approaches do folks have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-13-2020, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T04:04:17-07:00","id":1380899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380896#post1380896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Yet) Another question: how do folk feel about attribute spreads overall? For example, 5/5/1 gets you to a higher power tier far more quickly after only a few sessions of experience. It personally troubles me the least if social is primary (I can envisage someone who is, say, manipulative as all hell but not memorable easily), but the most with physical, where being a muscle-bound, hand-eye god who struggles to jog is a stretch until experience kicks in.<br /> <br /> Just take athletics and resistance as well I guess...<br /> <br /> What quirks/favoured approaches do folks have?</div> </div> </div> </div>At our table we use exp for Attributes instead of points (80/52/40 for Primary/Secondary/Tertiary). That way you can still make the 5/5/1 war god who can't jog if you want, BUT you can also make a 4/4/4 Olympian athlete. Similarly your Secondary can enjoy a 4/4/2 or 4/3/3 and your Tertiary can get 4/3/2 or 3/3/3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T04:28:56-07:00","id":1380904,"title":"","content":"With min-maxed attribute spreads, it's worth considering where you're actually aiming at.<br /> Because if you're trying to get to 5/5/5, sure... but most people won't. Most Solars who put xp into attributes are probably going to end up with like 4/4/5 and be happy with that. So that rather changes the metric.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T07:56:45-07:00","id":1380948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380767#post1380767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do, maybe give him the remaining Essence 1 charm from Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style (i.e. Demure Carp Feint), just to give him a little bit more interesting things to do in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380763#post1380763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It could be fun. Doo eet.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380906#post1380906\">It was disgustingly close.</a> Playing Sugar Daddy Captain as a PC protagonist, he Crashed the Immaculate (twice) and dealt 7 health levels of damage (the Earth Immaculate has 11 health levels) before the Immaculate knocked him unconcious.<br /> <br /> This is putting SDC on land, so most of his Sail Charms (including the critical Ship Claiming Stance) don't apply, in a white room, without the benefit of his fifty Followers backing him up.<br /> <br /> If I were running a one-on-one with Guybrush, I'd have him wake up aboard a ship, heading back to the Blessed Isle and give him the chance to talk his way free. Maybe have the Storm Mother from the last session attack the Immaculate's ship.<br /> <br /> But in a real game, I'm expecting at least two more Solar PCs. So I'd throw the other two Shikahri at them. I'd also expect at least one of them to be a <i>little </i>more invested in combat (2-5 combat charms including at least 1 Ox-Body Technique -- as per the explicit advice in the Staying Alive sidebar on page 126), and I'd expect the PCs to win.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not running this as a &quot;fair&quot; simulation of a fantasy world. I'm running it as I would run a game for friends.<br /> <br /> Guybrush is on the very lowest end of combat competancy that I advocate for, but he can still give Exalted NPCs a good fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-13-2020, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:24:20-07:00","id":1380990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in a real game, I'm expecting at least two more Solar PCs. So I'd throw the other two Shikahri at them. I'd also expect at least one of them to be a <i>little </i>more invested in combat (2-5 combat charms including at least 1 Ox-Body Technique -- as per the explicit advice in the Staying Alive sidebar on page 126), and I'd expect the PCs to win. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he was precisely designed to be part of a group of 3 solar PCs, one of whom is roughly similar at combat and one who is substantially better (War Supernal with the Command merit, a couple Melee charms, and artifact weapons and armor). They can probably do OK without all having Ox-Body Technique, as Blood and Salt Bondage gives a bunch of extra health levels, although I'm sure it would be wise to pick them up in case the ship is destroyed (though with their combined Sail charms that should not happen very often).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:38:45-07:00","id":1380996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380896#post1380896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Yet) Another question: how do folk feel about attribute spreads overall? For example, 5/5/1 gets you to a higher power tier far more quickly after only a few sessions of experience. It personally troubles me the least if social is primary (I can envisage someone who is, say, manipulative as all hell but not memorable easily), but the most with physical, where being a muscle-bound, hand-eye god who struggles to jog is a stretch until experience kicks in.<br /> <br /> Just take athletics and resistance as well I guess...<br /> <br /> What quirks/favoured approaches do folks have?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I took a page out of V5 and nixed primary/secondary/tertiary entirely in favor of a choice between a specialist/balanced/generalist spread with 9 scores each, assigned however the player wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:03:05-07:00","id":1381087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380996#post1380996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I took a page out of V5 and nixed primary/secondary/tertiary entirely in favor of a choice between a specialist/balanced/generalist spread with 9 scores each, assigned however the player wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool as is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25285_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25285\" data-vbnamecard=\"25285\">Epitome</a>'s XP solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380904#post1380904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With min-maxed attribute spreads, it's worth considering where you're actually aiming at.<br /> Because if you're trying to get to 5/5/5, sure... but most people won't. Most Solars who put xp into attributes are probably going to end up with like 4/4/5 and be happy with that. So that rather changes the metric.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience is those who do this are shooting for getting to 5/5/3 ASAP, anything after that is a bonus if the game lasts that long, and get there four sessions faster than a similarly investing 4/4/3. But, eh, that's the chargen minigame.<br /> <br /> I guess the major reason physical feels so much more of a thing (to me at least) than the other two is we as people generally have a much better idea of how the obviously measurable physical attributes are interconnected and how much of an outlier, say, a 1/5/5 spread would actually be (but if your concept is the most nimble, never say die street urchin or the wizened old sifu who you just can't kill then more power to you!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T17:39:27-07:00","id":1381150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380896#post1380896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any more details about the concept? Genuinely intrigued. If you've got loads of, say, larceny, then maybe the stealth charms don't matter so much?<br /> <br /> What are you taking instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>She didn't have Larcency charms before the cut down, just Stealth, some combat, and survival. After the cut down I plan to give her Deft Official's Way and Lock Opening Touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:11:38-07:00","id":1381341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1380502#post1380502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly any non-dawn or non-DB character that doesn't favour at least one, sometimes more than one, combat ability is basically unheard of.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are we counting as a combat ability here?<br /> <br /> I encourage players to at least get Dodge because there's a tendency for players to think of it as superhuman acrobatics (partially because a lot of RPGs that don't have a dedicated &quot;dodge&quot; skill tend to only factor it when someone's fast enough to dodge bullets, I'm from a horror RPG background where dodge tends to appear as a seperate trait to prevent all the PCs being blackbelts or award winning athletes, but I digress) when applying your evasion against an attack could be stunted as your character hurling themselves to the ground, moving behind cover or running away from people trying to kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:30:43-07:00","id":1381345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381341#post1381341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are we counting as a combat ability here?<br /> <br /> I encourage players to at least get Dodge because there's a tendency for players to think of it as superhuman acrobatics (partially because a lot of RPGs that don't have a dedicated &quot;dodge&quot; skill tend to only factor it when someone's fast enough to dodge bullets, I'm from a horror RPG background where dodge tends to appear as a seperate trait to prevent all the PCs being blackbelts or award winning athletes, but I digress) when applying your evasion against an attack could be stunted as your character hurling themselves to the ground, moving behind cover or running away from people trying to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some combination of effects to both attack and defend. So pure melee, pure MA, Archery + Dodge, MA + Dodge. Stuff like that. I've usually seen it taken as a given that you grab something like that at max, and then your actual combat ability is more measured in how many combat charms you take. <br /> <br /> So a Dawn is really combat capable because he has ten charms, whereas a kind of mediocre character will have Reed in the Wind, Drifting Leave Elusion, Shadow over Water, Wise Arrow, Sight Without Eyes, and Trance of Unhesitating Speed. Then a character who's not really so great will just have the excellencies, Wise Arrow and Reed in the Wind or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:48:45-07:00","id":1381352,"title":"","content":"Does anyone in this thread have thoughts on Merits? What Merits would you recommend to a starting character, beyond the obvious necessary ones for their character concept? Which would you recommend against taking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:30:50-07:00","id":1381363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381341#post1381341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I encourage players to at least get Dodge because there's a tendency for players to think of it as superhuman acrobatics (partially because a lot of RPGs that don't have a dedicated &quot;dodge&quot; skill tend to only factor it when someone's fast enough to dodge bullets, I'm from a horror RPG background where dodge tends to appear as a seperate trait to prevent all the PCs being blackbelts or award winning athletes, but I digress) when applying your evasion against an attack could be stunted as your character hurling themselves to the ground, moving behind cover or running away from people trying to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e seems to make this especially good advice, given rise from prone and disengage's dice pools. Those could easily have been athletics, but giving dodge something to do other than 'hit me if you can' seems a good idea. I like that you need to branch out to reliably accomplish those rolls \u2013 more skills the better really. Plus being able to run away quickly seems a good idea if you're not Captain I Kill Whatever Is In Front Of Me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381352#post1381352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone in this thread have thoughts on Merits? What Merits would you recommend to a starting character, beyond the obvious necessary ones for their character concept? Which would you recommend against taking?</div> </div> </div> </div>For fighting, most bang for your buck I would guess are probably artefacts, allies (or retainers, there was a conversation here about a DB just blowing their merit dots on this and effectively bringing something akin to a Cadet House to a battle) and command if you're big on war. Pain tolerance if you've spammed Ox-Bodies is pretty top-tier, if expensive. A lot of the 3-dot ones like Fast Reflexes seem like nice to haves, especially if you're optimised for alpha strikes, but are expensive for what they give you.<br /> <br /> I have a fondness for mentor, personally. Lotsa story and character development hooks. Oh, and sobriquet.<br /> <br /> <i>(Note: from only a small sample of real play 3e experience. Others will know better...).</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-14-2020, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:44:25-07:00","id":1381370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381345#post1381345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some combination of effects to both attack and defend. So pure melee, pure MA, Archery + Dodge, MA + Dodge. Stuff like that. I've usually seen it taken as a given that you grab something like that at max, and then your actual combat ability is more measured in how many combat charms you take.<br /> <br /> So a Dawn is really combat capable because he has ten charms, whereas a kind of mediocre character will have Reed in the Wind, Drifting Leave Elusion, Shadow over Water, Wise Arrow, Sight Without Eyes, and Trance of Unhesitating Speed. Then a character who's not really so great will just have the excellencies, Wise Arrow and Reed in the Wind or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't my experience 100% of the time.<br /> It is my experience... 90% of the time. (With Solars/DBs anyway. My Lunar game has one guy with Melee 5 and everyone else's combat abilities are 2 or 3. Obviously getting a combat ability to 5 is much more of an investment for less reward, for Lunars.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:56:11-07:00","id":1381372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381363#post1381363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For fighting, most bang for your buck I would guess are probably artefacts, allies (or retainers, there was a conversation here about a DB just blowing their merit dots on this and effectively bringing something akin to a Cadet House to a battle) and command if you're big on war. Pain tolerance if you've spammed Ox-Bodies is pretty top-tier, if expensive. A lot of the 3-dot ones like Fast Reflexes seem like nice to haves, especially if you're optimised for alpha strikes, but are expensive for what they give you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Familiar is another one. Spending 6 merit dots on a pair of Tyrant Lizards who join you in every battle and starting the fight by unleashing a pair of Terrifying Dragon Roars, backed by excellency boosted dicepools of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381370#post1381370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't my experience 100% of the time.<br /> It is my experience... 90% of the time. (With Solars/DBs anyway. My Lunar game has one guy with Melee 5 and everyone else's combat abilities are 2 or 3. Obviously getting a combat ability to 5 is much more of an investment for less reward, for Lunars.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen it not happen before in some cases, but almost never.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T11:05:57-07:00","id":1381375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381363#post1381363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For fighting, most bang for your buck I would guess are probably artefacts, allies (or retainers, there was a conversation here about a DB just blowing their merit dots on this and effectively bringing something akin to a Cadet House to a battle) and command if you're big on war. Pain tolerance if you've spammed Ox-Bodies is pretty top-tier, if expensive. A lot of the 3-dot ones like Fast Reflexes seem like nice to haves, especially if you're optimised for alpha strikes, but are expensive for what they give you.<br /> <br /> I have a fondness for mentor, personally. Lotsa story and character development hooks. Oh, and sobriquet.<br /> <br /> <i>(Note: from only a small sample of real play 3e experience. Others will know better...).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> I rewrote that ask a couple times and I realize now that I forgot to mention that I'm not interested in the most optimal ones, but in the ones that are the most fun to play with. Retainers and command are powerful but can be a headache to run in game. <br /> <br /> Artifacts definitely seem solid.<br /> <br /> Allies seems unpredictable to me - they could come up a lot or not at all.<br /> <br /> I was probably underrating Mentor, I will try to use it at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T12:29:23-07:00","id":1381397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381352#post1381352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone in this thread have thoughts on Merits? What Merits would you recommend to a starting character, beyond the obvious necessary ones for their character concept? Which would you recommend against taking?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're all good. (Except Demesne.)<br /> <br /> Personally, I have very specific thoughts about party NPCs. (They're a pain.) Retainers, Followers, Familiar and Command are great stunt fodder.<br /> <br /> Allies &amp; Mentor are great story hooks but need a lot of ST buy-in.<br /> <br /> Backing, Resources, Influence and Contacts are also great story hooks with less ST buy-in.<br /> <br /> Ambidextrous, Boundless Endurance, Direction Sense, Eidetic Memory, Hideous, Iron Stomach, Mighty Thew, Natural Immunity, Quick Draw, Selective Conception, Strong Lungs, Tempered by the Elements and Toxin Resistance are all fine choices if they fit your character concept. (Note on Mighty Thew: if you want it, buy it at character creation.)<br /> <br /> Danger Sense and Fast Reflexes are powerful combat options (provided your ST applies Danger Sense to Join Battle rolls -- personally, I'm disinclined).<br /> <br /> Pain Tolerance is hella expensive for what it does. (Personally, I think it's clear that it shouldn't reduce healing times, but if your ST disagrees then it's worth 4 dots easily.) But there are enough effects that reduce your wound penalties by one that you should consider it (especially if it's a significant upgrade to your Ox-Body).<br /> <br /> Martial Arts are often weaker than Native Charms. But you can buy them with Splat XP. Opening a vector to buy Charms with Splat XP is worth it. But...<br /> <br /> Artifact opens Evocations for Splat XP. Artifacts are also usually &quot;worth it&quot; even without Evocations. <br /> <br /> Hearthstone/Manse opens some neat tricks. Not too much work for your ST (which means how much fun they are is pretty much up to you). Demesne is a trap option you should never buy.<br /> <br /> Language is always worth it in the games I play. But if you're playing in one city with one language YMMV.<br /> <br /> Cult is half-price Willpower. And Willpower is great.<br /> <br /> Sobriquet is probably my favorite Merit. But I also kinda want to earn it in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T15:24:45-07:00","id":1381454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381397#post1381397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Note on Mighty Thew: if you want it, buy it at character creation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this? Am I not allowed to work out?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Martial Arts are often weaker than Native Charms. But you can buy them with Splat XP. Opening a vector to buy Charms with Splat XP is worth it. But... </div> </div> </div>This fits the impression I got - you should take Martial Arts if, and only if, it fits your character concept. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hearthstone/Manse opens some neat tricks. Not too much work for your ST (which means how much fun they are is pretty much up to you). Demesne is a trap option you should never buy. </div> </div> </div>What neat tricks are we talking here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Language is always worth it in the games I play. But if you're playing in one city with one language YMMV. </div> </div> </div>Even in a city with one language, High Realm might come in handy if the Realm controls your city or wants to control it (which is most cities in Creation...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cult is half-price Willpower. And Willpower is great. </div> </div> </div>I never thought about it like that, because it has such strong flavor implications, but now I want to try it sometime.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T15:46:21-07:00","id":1381457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381454#post1381454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What neat tricks are we talking here?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some like Jewel of the Rabbit's Sword which lets you once a day spend a willpower to reroll all 1s, pretty good even for Solars.<br /> <br /> For Lunars and DBs especially the Glory Sphere lets you learn one charm or evocation of a higher essence than you are currently. So at chargen a DB can pick up a signature charm, and then at Essence 4 you can grab a second signature.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381454#post1381454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never thought about it like that, because it has such strong flavor implications, but now I want to try it sometime.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes back at a different rate, which depending on the ST could be faster or slower than regular WP regen. On the other hand if you can somehow convince your ST that your Solar has a Cult 5 following, try also getting 10 willpower and just burn it like crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T16:18:37-07:00","id":1381466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381454#post1381454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is this? Am I not allowed to work out?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's talking about it from a purely optimization standpoint. If you buy the trait with XP, its cost scales. If you buy it with your initial allotment of Merits or even bonus points, it's just three points.<br /> <br /> \u200b(That said, it's not a huge difference. As a person who built a character who didn't have a single Attribute at 5 at chargen and has since raised the majority of them to 5, I don't feel my PC is especially weaker than the other player characters - just weaker than a hypothetical Perfect Parallel who only spends his points in the most optimal way possible, and is real smug to you about it afterward. And since he doesn't exist, it's not a problem.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T17:40:32-07:00","id":1381476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381457#post1381457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's some like Jewel of the Rabbit's Sword which lets you once a day spend a willpower to reroll all 1s, pretty good even for Solars.<br /> <br /> For Lunars and DBs especially the Glory Sphere lets you learn one charm or evocation of a higher essence than you are currently. So at chargen a DB can pick up a signature charm, and then at Essence 4 you can grab a second signature.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also Stone of Resilient Bamboo which gives +2 soak and doubles the speed at which you heal bashing damage for a 1m commitment, which is just a pretty cost efficient source of soak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381457#post1381457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts are often weaker than Native Charms. But you can buy them with Splat XP. Opening a vector to buy Charms with Splat XP is worth it. But...</div> </div> </div> </div>The 4 dot speedbump for martial arts also looks very questionable when you compare to the practically non-existent threshold for dipping your feet in sorcery. Which in-setting has always been portrayed as a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T18:15:44-07:00","id":1381491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381372#post1381372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spending 6 merit dots on a pair of Tyrant Lizards who join you in every battle</div> </div> </div> </div>Yoshi can't enter castles and Boo Houses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T18:54:11-07:00","id":1381500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381476#post1381476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 4 dot speedbump for martial arts also looks very questionable when you compare to the practically non-existent threshold for dipping your feet in sorcery. Which in-setting has always been portrayed as a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cheap for Solars, 3 Occult, no pre-req charms. For Lunars they need 4 previous mental attribute charms, and DBs need four Occult charms. The Lunar has to be already quite the cunning individual, and the DB must be a very accomplished Occultist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:08:32-07:00","id":1381544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381454#post1381454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is this? Am I not allowed to work out?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> At character creation, Mighty Thew costs the same as any other Merit. Three dot Mighty Thew costs three dots. Same as Fast Reflexes.<br /> <br /> With XP, 3 dot Fast Reflexes costs 9XP. Mighty Thew costs 15XP.<br /> <br /> It is the only Merit that scales its cost up this way. And that really sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T01:08:03-07:00","id":1381559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381500#post1381500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's cheap for Solars, 3 Occult, no pre-req charms. For Lunars they need 4 previous mental attribute charms, and DBs need four Occult charms. The Lunar has to be already quite the cunning individual, and the DB must be a very accomplished Occultist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unlike a 4 dot merit prequisite charms are usually actually good for something in themselves, and even the full-mooniest full-moon will soon enough get those 4 mental charms just from join-battle boosters.<br /> <br /> I was mainly thinking about solars though and how getting celestial circle sorcery is just 2 charms, which for investment is really just dipping your feet in something, while in-setting summoning 2nd-circles is a big deal even by celestial-exalt standards. Lunars at least require you to actually be invested in sorcery (5 terrestrial spells) to progress to the next circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:23:47-07:00","id":1381629,"title":"","content":"Mighty Thew: Wow! I would probably houserule that, if it ever came up, to let my players become swole if they want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381500#post1381500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's cheap for Solars, 3 Occult, no pre-req charms. For Lunars they need 4 previous mental attribute charms, and DBs need four Occult charms. The Lunar has to be already quite the cunning individual, and the DB must be a very accomplished Occultist.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Occult were a random ability we would expect ~40% of Solars to have at least a 3 in Occult at character creation, and from a pure optimization perspective they all should take Terrestrial Circle Sorcery - it just offers so much for so little investment. (I'm partial to taking Stormwind Rider as a control spell, and then Travel Without Distance when you get Celestial, because they offer great long-range movement options, which are hard to get from other Charms in Exalted.) In practice I think people mostly only take significant Occult if they're planning to make their character a Sorcerer based on character concept.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the Terrestrial Circle Sorcery charm just got you Sorcerous Workings and the other incidental abilities, and you had to take another Charm to cast a spell, would people say that this is underpowered or doesn't reflect how difficult it is to acquire Sorcery in the fiction?<br /> <br /> This is basically what Martial Arts is - a Charm's worth of investment before you get to the good stuff - except the good stuff in Sorcery is more unique, and this first Charm would still get you totally unique abilities. <br /> <br /> Thus I think the character building system pushes you away from taking Martial Arts and towards taking Sorcery, whereas based on the fiction it should probably be the reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T07:22:51-07:00","id":1381639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381454#post1381454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What neat tricks are we talking here?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about &quot;not dying from physical harm, ever&quot; and &quot;regenerating faster than a Lunar with a maxed investment in Stamina&quot;? (The Gem of Incomparable Wellness was a mistake.)<br /> <br /> Other standouts include the Ivy-Hilt Gemstone (Disarm gambits against you have +2 Difficulty, effectively making them far too risky and expensive to ever be worth it), the Key of Mastery (for the low low price of just one Evocation, gain the control effect on one of your spells, a bonus you can even swap between stories), the Stone of Aquatic Prowess (all the benefits of being a Water Aspect for just two Evocations! too bad you could do a sorcerous working to gain Gills 3 with Subtlety for a fraction of the cost) and the Seven Leaping Dragons Stone (gain 2i whenever you switch MA Forms reflexively; at this point, I think we have enough styles for this to be effectively +2i/round for free on average).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T08:55:06-07:00","id":1381655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381629#post1381629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Occult were a random ability we would expect ~40% of Solars to have at least a 3 in Occult at character creation,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested as to how you got to this figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-15-2020, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T09:04:32-07:00","id":1381659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381476#post1381476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 4 dot speedbump for martial arts also looks very questionable when you compare to the practically non-existent threshold for dipping your feet in sorcery. Which in-setting has always been portrayed as a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery is a bit of an outlier given that artifacts are priced partially in terms of how much of your reward xp you can funnel into them.<br /> I think a factor here is that while you could invest a whole MA's worth of reward xp into sorcery, the end result is likely to end up as a massive list of unrelated powers competing for your attention rather than building upon what those before it allowed you to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T11:15:37-07:00","id":1381711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381655#post1381655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm interested as to how you got to this figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you focus on your caste and favored abilities, you have 28 points to spend on those 10 abilities, so almost all of them get a 3. You could go lower if you put a lot of 1s and 2s into unfavored abilities, though. Then with bonus points you could get more 3s, so 10 3s is probably not too much of an overestimate. 10/25 = 40%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:39:29-07:00","id":1381742,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... actually, I'd probably say 40% of Solar PCs I see do indeed have Occult 3+, though I'd say sorcerers are more like 20% of Solar PCs. A lot of people have Occult 3 and the two charms for fighting spirits and that's it.<br /> May just be my group though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the end result is likely to end up as a massive list of unrelated powers competing for your attention rather than building upon what those before it allowed you to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true.<br /> My celestial sorcerers (of which I've played 3; a Solar and 2 Lunars) always felt like they had a lot of different quite useful things they could do with sorcery, rather than a few really, really good things. Whereas, say, the Night PCs feel like they're really, really good at fighting and sneaking, the Twilights like they're really good at crafting and medicine, but not that they have cool/strange powers for a lot of different situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:45:35-07:00","id":1381746,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth. In the Arena thread I have a Solar Dawn named Shining Topaz. I could definitely see her getting Ghost Eating Technique. But I could never see her getting sorcery.<br /> <br /> Sometimes Sorcery is just the wrong choice for the character, even if they meet the minimums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:55:47-07:00","id":1381747,"title":"","content":"Yeah, exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T13:12:09-07:00","id":1381751,"title":"","content":"Sorcery is also probably too good for what the cost is, and was maybe an over correction from 2e where being a Sorcerer was a lot of investment for not a heck of a good return mechanically. It hasn't been a massive problem at my table, but I've definitely seen a few characters that suspiciously have nothing in their concept or backstory that makes them seem like a sorcerer, but have it anyway, usually with Summon Demon and Skin of Bronze or Dragon Claw as their only spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T13:40:16-07:00","id":1381759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381659#post1381659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery is a bit of an outlier given that artifacts are priced partially in terms of how much of your reward xp you can funnel into them.<br /> I think a factor here is that while you could invest a whole MA's worth of reward xp into sorcery, the end result is likely to end up as a massive list of unrelated powers competing for your attention rather than building upon what those before it allowed you to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really talking about grabbing a bunch of spells. ISoB (Control) + Demon of the First Circle is really all you need, then eventually one control + demon summoning for Celestial and Solar if you ever get there.<br /> <br /> The rest of your solar xp you can throw on workings, which you can all go in the same direction untill you ST starts limiting downtime just to keep you from derailing the game.<br /> <br /> Most extreme at E3 it's 8xp (one MA charm) for a custom-designed minion equal in power to a 2nd-circle demon (xp which by the working rules you get back if it's destroyed or turns against you).<br /> <br /> For the price of one full martial art you can have a squad of custom-designed minions as tough as Octavian and/or as reality-warping as Sigereth solving all your problems for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T16:41:47-07:00","id":1381796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381759#post1381759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest of your solar xp you can throw on workings, which you can all go in the same direction untill you ST starts limiting downtime just to keep you from derailing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a great tactic if you can expect your fellow players and the Storyteller to put everything on hold until you've got what you need to win.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T16:45:23-07:00","id":1381800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381759#post1381759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the price of one full martial art you can have a squad of custom-designed minions as tough as Octavian and/or as reality-warping as Sigereth solving all your problems for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are really good you won't have to play the game at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:01:17-07:00","id":1381810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381796#post1381796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a great tactic if you can expect your fellow players and the Storyteller to put everything on hold until you've got what you need to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did note that the ST will limit you (in some way) to keep you from derailing the game. Which he should, because 'I solve all my problems with my army of magic super-bots' is overpowered in any game with the many months of downtime the rules seem to assume given training times and such (and even worse it's pretty boring).<br /> <br /> But you were arguing that the power sorcery can give you isn't that likely to be that significant in any particular area and mostly constituted a collection of neat tricks, then when I point out what it as written can do some crazy powerfull things in basically any area you go 'oh but then your ST will stop you', which kind of indicates the power sorcery was indeed rather high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-15-2020, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:06:08-07:00","id":1381814,"title":"","content":"I didn't think of it before, but I wonder if the large prerequisites for DBs and Lunars to get Sorcery are not because they're supposed to be weaker, but because the writers realised how many Solars were taking Sorcery when it wasn't really part of their concept because you get so much for 1 prequisite-less charm... ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:08:44-07:00","id":1381815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381759#post1381759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really talking about grabbing a bunch of spells. ISoB (Control) + Demon of the First Circle is really all you need, then eventually one control + demon summoning for Celestial and Solar if you ever get there.<br /> <br /> The rest of your solar xp you can throw on workings, which you can all go in the same direction untill you ST starts limiting downtime just to keep you from derailing the game.<br /> <br /> Most extreme at E3 it's 8xp (one MA charm) for a custom-designed minion equal in power to a 2nd-circle demon (xp which by the working rules you get back if it's destroyed or turns against you).<br /> <br /> For the price of one full martial art you can have a squad of custom-designed minions as tough as Octavian and/or as reality-warping as Sigereth solving all your problems for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't really do that &quot;on the side&quot; though. You'll have to look for rare means, which will send you on quests, which will force you to use your army, which will reveal said army to the world, which will turn the world against you. Basically the entire Campaign becomes about your personal god-spirit army.<br /> <br /> Much like a Crafter who tries to &quot;win&quot; by chugging out Artifacts like a factory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:26:16-07:00","id":1381819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381815#post1381815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll have to look for rare means, which will send you on quests<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You really don't have to, Cooperation + a complimentary ability or spell is enough to quite confidently finish an ambition 3 finesse 5 celestial working in 7 weeks.<br /> <br /> Now again your ST of course can say you have to and it'll be a cooler story if you do, but those aren't the rules for sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381814#post1381814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't think of it before, but I wonder if the large prerequisites for DBs and Lunars to get Sorcery are not because they're supposed to be weaker, but because the writers realised how many Solars were taking Sorcery when it wasn't really part of their concept because you get so much for 1 prequisite-less charm... ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this is the case.<br /> <br /> If I ever run a solar game again I'm definitiely house-ruling in some pre-requisite Terrestrial spells to grab Celestial Circle the way it is for Lunars, and a few celestial spells for Solar Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-15-2020, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:47:43-07:00","id":1381825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381810#post1381810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did note that the ST will limit you (in some way) to keep you from derailing the game. Which he should, because 'I solve all my problems with my army of magic super-bots' is overpowered in any game with the many months of downtime the rules seem to assume given training times and such (and even worse it's pretty boring).<br /> <br /> But you were arguing that the power sorcery can give you isn't that likely to be that significant in any particular area and mostly constituted a collection of neat tricks, then when I point out what it as written can do some crazy powerfull things in basically any area you go 'oh but then your ST will stop you', which kind of indicates the power sorcery was indeed rather high.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crafting and Workings will let you take over the world with unlimited time and no obstacles.<br /> <br /> I'm actively uncomfortable with framing the limitations of that as &quot;the Storyteller will limit you&quot; like it's an invocation of a Storyteller's Rule veto, rather than the normal game condition of the Storyteller telling story and the other players wanting to do stuff with their characters, mostly because my experience is that the person whose able to operate around such considerations is someone the group is worried about upsetting for out of character reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:59:31-07:00","id":1381828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381815#post1381815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't really do that &quot;on the side&quot; though. You'll have to look for rare means, which will send you on quests, which will force you to use your army, which will reveal said army to the world, which will turn the world against you. Basically the entire Campaign becomes about your personal god-spirit army.<br /> <br /> Much like a Crafter who tries to &quot;win&quot; by chugging out Artifacts like a factory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am becoming increasingly convinced that an all-sorcerers campaign is the best way to explore sorcerous workings, summoning, and their consequences - basically because they're most interesting when you are spending the whole campaign thinking about them, which is only fair if everyone gets to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T18:12:58-07:00","id":1381835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381825#post1381825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crafting and Workings will let you take over the world with unlimited time and no obstacles.<br /> <br /> I'm actively uncomfortable with framing the limitations of that as &quot;the Storyteller will limit you&quot; like it's an invocation of a Storyteller's Rule veto, rather than the normal game condition of the Storyteller telling story and the other players wanting to do stuff with their characters, mostly because my experience is that the person whose able to operate around such considerations is someone the group is worried about upsetting for out of character reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't actually need to stop anyone from doing anything with their characters more than someone who wants to raise an attribute does though? Actually said working requires less time even than raising an attribute from 1 to 2, and time is really the only thing the rules demand.<br /> <br /> I might be in a minority having been in a game that followed the rules for training times but if your game spans the years it kinda has too for them to work, throwing in a few workings during that time is not really an imposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-15-2020, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T18:33:56-07:00","id":1381840,"title":"","content":"Training Martial Arts doesn't cause a rain of stones; or statues to bleed; or sacrificial victims at the temples, lacking their hearts and livers, to escape the bloodstained altars after the knife lays them open. Training Martial Arts won't make ten black vultures circle the Bastion for nine evenings running; or make astrologers cease readings for fear of their lives. Training your Martial Arts won't make the ivy on the outer ramparts give way to a creeper which appears black in all but the most intense sunlight.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt only takes a Difficulty 3 roll to realize that a sorcerous working is being undertaken in your area; if you can get <i>five</i> successes on the roll, you can pinpoint it to its <i>exact </i>location. (Maybe check the Necropolitan Hill, where lightning smote the tomb out of a clear sky?) Shave another one off those Difficulties if you're a sorcerer yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-15-2020, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T19:07:34-07:00","id":1381844,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's the prospect of a new Sorcerous Working being enacted for every martial arts charm or evocation your circlemates are learning that's raising a red flag, not &quot;a few workings&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T21:55:16-07:00","id":1381858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381835#post1381835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't actually need to stop anyone from doing anything with their characters more than someone who wants to raise an attribute does though? Actually said working requires less time even than raising an attribute from 1 to 2, and time is really the only thing the rules demand.<br /> <br /> I might be in a minority having been in a game that followed the rules for training times but if your game spans the years it kinda has too for them to work, throwing in a few workings during that time is not really an imposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The training times in the book are the worst case scenario, when you literally don't stop questing or have any downtime. If you're stopping the campaign for 2 months for a Working, then in most cases your allies will complete their training much faster than you will complete your working since they're not doing anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core p.178</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">these training times assume that characters balance their training time with getting other things done\u2014a character who retreats from her other duties to pursue nothing but training could raise her traits significantly faster than the times given here.</div> </div> </div> </div>At any rate, Exalted is nothing if not loaded with exploits that make you invincible and/or unstoppable, all kosher and within the rules-as-written (e.g. flying archers, mass summoners, drain-willpower-so-social-influence-always-succeeds build, etc). If that's the sort of thing people dig at your table then by all means go crazy, but it can very easily ruin games when not everybody at the table is on board with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 04-16-2020, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T02:03:56-07:00","id":1381872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381858#post1381858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">flying archers</div> </div> </div> </div>Turns out that those can be put on a level playing field by being in a place with a low enough ceiling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381858#post1381858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mass summoners</div> </div> </div> </div>She only gets one demon per night, and <i>if</i> a Celestial sorcerer, then once a month she can substitute one of those demons for a stronger demon (at the cost of having to spend an additional Willpower). So after a month or two of dedicated summoning, she has a Size 2 battle group with Poor Drill and Might 2, plus or minus one or two powerful lieutenants. And in the meantime, she's got to herd cats (both metaphorically and possibly literally), because even with their indelible Defining Intimacy toward her, demons are still living things with minds and desires..<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't envy her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381858#post1381858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">drain-willpower-so-social-influence-always-succeeds build</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet persuasion attempts that don't key off an existing Intimacy <i>still fail</i>; no Willpower is needed to reject it. A Presence 5 fast-talker <i>cannot </i>influence me to put myself in danger for him if he offers me nothing and I hate him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-16-2020, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T05:34:35-07:00","id":1381901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381858#post1381858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At any rate, Exalted is nothing if not loaded with exploits that make you invincible and/or unstoppable, all kosher and within the rules-as-written (e.g. flying archers, mass summoners, drain-willpower-so-social-influence-always-succeeds build, etc). If that's the sort of thing people dig at your table then by all means go crazy, but it can very easily ruin games when not everybody at the table is on board with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you trying to frame this as me being pro cheesy exploits?<br /> <br /> People said sorcery was not that powerfull, I pointed out that sorcery actually has cheesy-exploit level power. Then you go 'boo cheesy exploiter', which in itself contradicts the idea that sorcery is not really powerfull if thats your reaction.<br /> <br /> (For the record the one time I ever actually used the create 2nd-circle equivalent construct working was to create a guardian to defend our city-state while we were otherwise occupied.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-16-2020, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T06:10:57-07:00","id":1381903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381901#post1381901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why are you trying to frame this as me being pro cheesy exploits?<br /> <br /> People said sorcery was not that powerfull, I pointed out that sorcery actually has cheesy-exploit level power. Then you go 'boo cheesy exploiter', which in itself contradicts the idea that sorcery is not really powerfull if thats your reaction.<br /> <br /> (For the record the one time I ever actually used the create 2nd-circle equivalent construct working was to create a guardian to defend our city-state while we were otherwise occupied.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, I completely missed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381810#post1381810\">this post</a> you wrote in the discussion. Without the added context it provides I got the mistaken impression that you were defending the mass workings strategy from criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T08:55:16-07:00","id":1381931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381901#post1381901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People said sorcery was not that powerfull, I pointed out that sorcery actually has cheesy-exploit level power. Then you go 'boo cheesy exploiter', which in itself contradicts the idea that sorcery is not really powerfull if thats your reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that wasn't the point I was making at all. Lets go back to what I wrote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381659#post1381659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery is a bit of an outlier given that artifacts are priced partially in terms of how much of your reward xp you can funnel into them.<br /> I think a factor here is that while you could invest a whole MA's worth of reward xp into sorcery, the end result is likely to end up as a massive list of unrelated powers competing for your attention rather than building upon what those before it allowed you to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon of the First Circle is really powerful with even a little time to prepare and I'm pretty sure nobody's arguing otherwise. But, you don't get the option to invest another 50-60 Reward Xp on getting better at summoning first circle demons because spells* don't work that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Evocations however do, a demonic themed sorcerous relic absolutely could enhance your ability to summon demons, <b>but </b>at chargen you'd be paying merit dots for the ability to learn charms much like you would with a martial art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-16-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T11:05:41-07:00","id":1382201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1381759#post1381759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really talking about grabbing a bunch of spells. ISoB (Control) + Demon of the First Circle is really all you need, then eventually one control + demon summoning for Celestial and Solar if you ever get there.<br /> <br /> The rest of your solar xp you can throw on workings, which you can all go in the same direction untill you ST starts limiting downtime just to keep you from derailing the game.<br /> <br /> Most extreme at E3 it's 8xp (one MA charm) for a custom-designed minion equal in power to a 2nd-circle demon (xp which by the working rules you get back if it's destroyed or turns against you).<br /> <br /> <i><b>For the price of one full martial art you can have a squad of custom-designed minions as tough as Octavian and/or as reality-warping as Sigereth solving all your problems for you</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which Seems exceptionally boring to Me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T11:56:29-07:00","id":1382212,"title":"","content":"Last session, I thought, hmmm, the Dragonblood compound I've been watching is guarded by a few bird spirits and a lion-dog in the spirit world. I should summon up a demon-spider so that if I end up attacking the compound, I can send it to distract the spirits and keep them off my back. But... ah, they're such a hassle. You've basically got to babysit the damn things or they'll no doubt get into some trouble. Laying eggs that hatch into eerie demon-tales, or eating priests, or whatever. And Kovan is an Essence 5 Lunar wizard, how useful is a first-circle demon going to be in a fight with anything that's a challenge for him?<br /> And in the end... I'm glad I didn't bother, because I had to stop watching the compound and go to a soiree at the Perfect's palace anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> My experience with sorcery, having played 3 celestial sorcerers, is that you have a bunch of individual powers which don't really combine well, but are each quite useful in unusual circumstances. Most of my spells I actually very rarely used, but when I did use them they were very effective. Combat spells you can use a lot if you're a combat-sorcerer, but combat-sorcery isn't actually that good (except vs battle groups). Transport spells and communication spells on the other hand are used so damn much that they eat up all your willpower! (Which is why my second sorcerer didn't know any.)<br /> <br /> One of my friends played a Solar sorcerer who did a ton of workings. And these workings did all sorts of amazing things. But... they do cost xp. I think he spent 60xp on workings. Actually, some of the other players thought that character was by far the most powerful, with her wings and her heart of fire and all her dragons and golems and nation of magical Melniboneans. Whereas the player felt that she actually wasn't that great (except for Death Ray, which was basically how she fought 60% of her fights), because of putting so much xp into workings, making the character weaker in her own capabilities in any short-term situations we found ourselves in (because workings do take a long time, even for a Solar sorcerer with 20+ dice). Because workings do have weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, saying all this, yes absolutely it is a very strong yet (generally, not always) unthematic choice for a Dawn to take Occult 3, Terrestrial sorcery and Invulnerable Skin of Bronze as a control spell. But I think that's because Invulnerable Skin of Bronze (as a control spell) is maybe just a bit too good.<br /> <br /> In terms of Demons, there is the issue that you probably want maxed-out pools or your demon may escape, and that is an investment... but then, it's not a big investment.<br /> <br /> Not, saying all this, that I would complain if Sorcery needed 4 Occult or Lore charms as a prerequisite or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T13:31:31-07:00","id":1382229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1382212#post1382212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of Demons, there is the issue that you probably want maxed-out pools or your demon may escape, and that is an investment... but then, it's not a big investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with Int 2, Occ 3 you'll successfully bind a resolve 3 Demon of the 1st circle almost 9 times out of 10 if you use your excellency and it's almost 19 times out of 20 if you stunt as well. Given the the most likely result of failing is having to spend another 4 motes (so you don't flare your anima beyond your caste mark) to banish it I think the primary problem of a low Occult Solar summoner is keeping the behavior of your bound demons in check rather than the 1 in 100s chance of setting a unbound demon loose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T13:39:22-07:00","id":1382231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Speedbump</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1382229#post1382229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with Int 2, Occ 3 you'll successfully bind a resolve 3 Demon of the 1st circle almost 9 times out of 10 if you use your excellency and it's almost 19 times out of 20 if you stunt as well. Given the the most likely result of failing is having to spend another 4 motes (so you don't flare your anima beyond your caste mark) to banish it I think the primary problem of a low Occult Solar summoner is keeping the behavior of your bound demons in check rather than the 1 in 100s chance of setting a unbound demon loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also if you're a circle of Solars a single bloodape isn't really even worth busting the dice out for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T13:51:40-07:00","id":1382235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1382231#post1382231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also if you're a circle of Solars a single bloodape isn't really even worth busting the dice out for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yea, but if the failure chance were higher you might actually have to worry about what that immaterial Agata that took one look at the Dawn and flew off would get up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T21:32:44-07:00","id":1382285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1382212#post1382212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience with sorcery, having played 3 celestial sorcerers, is that you have a bunch of individual powers which don't really combine well, but are each quite useful in unusual circumstances. Most of my spells I actually very rarely used, but when I did use them they were very effective. Combat spells you can use a lot if you're a combat-sorcerer, but combat-sorcery isn't actually that good (except vs battle groups). Transport spells and communication spells on the other hand are used so damn much that they eat up all your willpower! (Which is why my second sorcerer didn't know any.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wondered how the Brilliant Raptor Sniper Combat sorceror build worked in real play. If you have a high enough Willpower, you can launch 10+ damage decisives around every other turn from base Init, did you ever see one or get to play one?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T02:46:37-07:00","id":1382297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Speedbump</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1382229#post1382229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with Int 2, Occ 3 you'll successfully bind a resolve 3 Demon of the 1st circle almost 9 times out of 10 if you use your excellency and it's almost 19 times out of 20 if you stunt as well. Given the the most likely result of failing is having to spend another 4 motes (so you don't flare your anima beyond your caste mark) to banish it I think the primary problem of a low Occult Solar summoner is keeping the behavior of your bound demons in check rather than the 1 in 100s chance of setting a unbound demon loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realise it was that easy.<br /> Sigh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T02:48:21-07:00","id":1382298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1382285#post1382285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always wondered how the Brilliant Raptor Sniper Combat sorceror build worked in real play. If you have a high enough Willpower, you can launch 10+ damage decisives around every other turn from base Init, did you ever see one or get to play one?<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't.<br /> Combine it with the Ifrit-initiation and have it as a control spell and it's even better.<br /> <br /> Still, any combat style that doesn't involve gaining initiative is a risky one, due to crash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T08:45:40-07:00","id":1413975,"title":"","content":"So I was wondering if I could get some help tuning a potential PC. I want to play a str focused supernatural Ath night caste. As such, he's looking at Str 5 and Mighty Thews 3 to start, along with Giant (doesn't actually make him stronger, but fits the Concept and might let him explain away some charms). He's probably looking at grapple brawl. Is Brawl 5 with dex 3 going to be basically fine, or will it mean he's trivializing combat encounters? Besides Brawl, he's probably looking at Ath 5 (Strength). Assume he wants to be able to beat up some dudes, maybe a DB or wrestle something suitability beefy. I'm not trying to make Invincible Punch Dude, here (or I'd be playing a Brawl Dawn), but it's important that his Str is basically Unmatched. And actually getting to hit or grab people is kind of important to making him more than just 'the guy who whiffs all the time'. Also, I'm debating where to put his Stamina. Another 5 is affordable, and fits the mental image, as well as making Resistance charms work better. Tentatively, he's probably taking Iron Skin Concentration, 1 Ox-Body, Vicious Lunge, Devil Strangling Attitude, and Armor Eating Strike. Too many combat charms? 3 defensive, 3 offensive, and a Ox-Body?<br /> <br /> Edit: Most of my previous experience is in prior editions, so I am under the impression that soak and resistance are generally worse than not getting hit, and that dex is the combat stat that really makes a difference. Please let me know if these assumptions need to be updated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-16-2020, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T08:58:03-07:00","id":1413976,"title":"","content":"Dex 3 Brawl 5 and 7 Charms will put you solidly in the mid-tier in a typical group. You <i>will </i>demolish officially-statted opponents (but this is a feature). However, if your group is very light on combat-capable characters, you might want to drop your Brawl score by a dot or two (swapping Devil-Strangling Attitude for Fists of Iron or Thunderclap Rush Attack as you no longer qualify).<br /> <br /> Mind that a lot of opponents don't really have an answer to a 20 dice grapple followed by 20 dice on control followed by a Slam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 09-16-2020, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T09:24:36-07:00","id":1413977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1413976#post1413976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if your group is very light on combat-capable characters, you might want to drop your Brawl score by a dot or two (swapping Devil-Strangling Attitude for Fists of Iron or Thunderclap Rush Attack as you no longer qualify).</div> </div> </div> </div>Got to talk to the ST and the other players, but : What if I reduced dex to 2 and kept Brawl at 5? My inner self is cringing at trying to fight with dex 2, but that would leave me with a parry of 4. And still let me grapple with Str.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1413976#post1413976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind that a lot of opponents don't really have an answer to a 20 dice grapple followed by 20 dice on control followed by a Slam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a thing? I'm still wrapping my head around generous charm use without a defensive combo, but blowing 20 motes like that seems ... unwise. Combat drip will bring 5 back, but that seems like a really, really big expenditure, and kind of leaves me hanging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T13:09:08-07:00","id":1414022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1413977#post1413977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a thing? I'm still wrapping my head around generous charm use without a defensive combo, but blowing 20 motes like that seems ... unwise. Combat drip will bring 5 back, but that seems like a really, really big expenditure, and kind of leaves me hanging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here's a list of all the antagonists from the corebook, all the Dragonblooded from What Fire has Wrought, and a selection of guys from Adversaries of the Righteous and Hundred Devil Night Parade. <b>Bold </b>are characters who either have, or can use essence to boost, their defenses above 5. <u><b>Bold and underline</b></u> are the ones that can do it above 8.<br /> <br /> Corebook<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 2 Brigand<br /> 4 Battle Troop<br /> 4 Horse Archer<br /> 4 Grizzled Merc<br /> 5 Elite Bodyguard<br /> 5 Bride of Alhat<br /> 3 Siganese Deathspeaker<br /> 4 Monk<br /> 4 Assassin<br /> 2 Snakefolk Merchant<br /> 4 Jade Statue<br /> 4 Fog Shark<br /> 5 Mist the Revolutionary<br /> 2 Zombie<br /> 4 Hungry Ghost<br /> 3 Honoured Ancestor<br /> 4 War Ghost<br /> 5 Mortwight<br /> 4 Bonesider<br /> <b>6 Nephwrack</b><br /> 5 Disease Spirit<br /> 4 Dog of the Unbroken Earth<br /> 4 Field Guardian<br /> 4 Storm Mother<br /> <b><u>6 Alhat, God of Southern War and Cattle</u><br /> 6 Garda Bird</b><br /> 5 Greenmaw<br /> 4 Tidemere<br /> 3 Vaktri<br /> <u><b>7 Fakharu, Censor of the West</b></u><br /> 5 Agata<br /> 4 Blood Ape<br /> 4 Neomah<br /> <b>6 Aluva Keeper of the Forge of Night<br /> <u>7 Octavian, the Living Tower, QUarter Prince of Hell</u></b><br /> 5 Sigareth, the Player of Games<br /> <b>7 Fair Folk Cataphract</b><br /> 5 Fair Folk Lorelei<br /> 5 Hobgoblin<br /> 5 Silverwight<br /> 5 Buck-Ogre<br /> 5 Manticore<br /> <b>4-6 Young Dynast<br /> 5-7 Air Monk<br /> <u>6-9 Earth monk<br /> 6-9 Fire Monk</u><br /> 5-7 Earth General<br /> 4-8 Lunar Warlord<br /> 4-8 Lunar Trickster<br /> 6 Sidereal Assassin<br /> <u>6-11 Deathknight</u><br /> 4-7 Liminal Ghosthunter<br /> 4-7 Exigent Exalt</b><br /> 3 Angler Lizard<br /> 4 Armored Terror<br /> 3 Bear<br /> 3 Benthic Knifetooth<br /> 5 Boar Tusk Crocodile<br /> 3 Bunyip<br /> 4 Claw Strider<br /> 3 Death Moa<br /> 4 Wolf<br /> 4 Eagle<br /> 4 Emperor Sloth<br /> 4 Gorilla<br /> 4 Great Cat<br /> 3 Hellboar<br /> 3 Evasion<br /> 4 Ox-Dragon<br /> 2 Pestletail<br /> 4 Quoll-Lion<br /> 4 River Dragon<br /> 5 Siege Lizard<br /> <b>6 Tyrant Lizard</b><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> WFHW<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>4-6 Amon Mora House head for the Imperial Palace<br /> <u>6-9 Berit, General, Daughter of the Empress<br /> 6-9 Cathak Cainen, house matriarch for house Cathak</u><br /> 5-8 Cynis Cogen<br /> 4-6 Ledaal Kes, agent of the All Seeing Eye<br /> 5-7 Mnemon, Matriarch of House Mnemon, daughter of the Empress<br /> 4-6 Ragara Benoru, Leader of the Bloody Scythe rebellion, magistrate of the Empress<br /> 4-6 Sesus Nagezzer, The Slug, former soldier, information broker<br /> <u>6-9 Tepet Ejeva, The Roseblack, General of the Vermillion Legion</u></b><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Adversaries and Devil Night Parade<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 5 Adeimantus, Custodian of Utopia<br /> 4 Isabet Maken, Master of Cauldron Valley<br /> <b>6 Iron Siaka, Chosen of Serenity</b><br /> 4 Bosocu, Prodigal Son of the Swamps<br /> 3 Fivefold Masks and Lies, Servent of Chaos<br /> 4 Afhonda, Lady of the Well<br /> 5 Ashana Ikatu, Master of Coiled Viper Dojo, First of Night's Talons<br /> <b>5-7 Ku Nenaveya, Captain of the Blue Wolves, Wielder fo Frozen Heart</b><br /> 4 Peremuz Rogue Homunculus<br /> 4 Ixer who Dreams for the Dead<br /> <b>5-8 Odara, Chosen of Ash, Captain of Kalaho Ahn</b><br /> 3-5 The Bloodthirsty, scourge of Wavecrest<br /> 5 Sentinal Fern<br /> 2 Ghostfisher<br /> 4 Eight Tailed Mole Rat<br /> 4 Barrow Hound<br /> 4 Dreamhawk<br /> 3 Haunt<br /> 3 Aughdeighe<br /> <b>6 Armored Kraken</b><br /> 4 Jungle Stalker<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sadly I don't have time to go through more of Adversaries and Devil Night Parade, but I can assure you that what's shown in the snippet I have there is representative of the spread. It might even be a bit weighted towards the high end.<br /> <br /> <br /> With Dex 3, Brawl 5 and a specialty, your base attack pool is 13, with a full excellency it's 21, and with a stunt it's 23. That hits a defense of 5 literally 99% of the time. it hits a defense of 8 90% of the time, and a defense of 11 60% of the time. Which is also assuming that the thing you're facing is not suffering from any defense penalties due to environment, wound penalties, or onslaught penalties. Unlike 2e your Defense doesn't refresh from onslaught penalties until your turn comes around again, so as long as somebody else attacked the thing you're attacking, you'll be benefiting from onslaught.<br /> <br /> Oh and likewise the things there that have like 3-5 as their best defense tend to have attack pools of 6-10. So your parry of 5 with Dex 3, Brawl 5, and a specialty, boosted by motes up to 9, that's going to be a 5% chance for somebody with a dicepool of 10 to hit you with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, some of this will depend on what your ST and the rest of your group is doing. I've talked to somebody who was in a DB game and the only thing they ever rolled Join Battle against was high powered celestial exalted. If that's what you're doing this huge list doesn't mean much. If you're fighting anything close to an average spread of enemies though your statline will <i>crush </i>the opposition, and the only things you'll even remotely struggle against are people like a directional war god, or a literal mile high behemoth that can crush cities with a single footstep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-16-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T13:35:11-07:00","id":1414031,"title":"","content":"That's sort of why I'm asking. I want to be able to wrestle an Earth Immaculate, with at least a good chance of success. I don't need to be able tell Ahlat 'stop hitting yourself'.<br /> <br /> If the expectation is that I'm supposed to be throwing out 8-10 motes on every attack, and then again on my control roll (and maybe to get my parry higher than 5, so I can be in bold on your list) that changes things significantly. But I'm under the impression that I'll need a round or two of withering attacks to be able to land that decisive grapple Gambit. And I'll be losing either motes or initiative (or both) every time I get attacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:19:57-07:00","id":1414046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1414031#post1414031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's sort of why I'm asking. I want to be able to wrestle an Earth Immaculate, with at least a good chance of success. I don't need to be able tell Ahlat 'stop hitting yourself'.<br /> <br /> If the expectation is that I'm supposed to be throwing out 8-10 motes on every attack, and then again on my control roll (and maybe to get my parry higher than 5, so I can be in bold on your list) that changes things significantly. But I'm under the impression that I'll need a round or two of withering attacks to be able to land that decisive grapple Gambit. And I'll be losing either motes or initiative (or both) every time I get attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, more Dex is still always best (it dictates so many things, like disengage) but 3e has made it less crucial to Exalted than it's ever previously been, especially for Solar Brawl.<br /> <br /> Bear with me: Solars can get solid initiative off Join Battle rolls right out of the gate. You'll then be able to wither for initiative as part of a grapple (check out savaging attacks on page 201 of the Core book). With the kind of dice pool you're talking, against most foes one-on-one there's an excellent chance you'll establish control for several turns, savage once to build some more initiative and then slam them into the deck, forsaking remaining rounds of control to do a &amp;^%$ tonne of damage (Solar Brawl is very, very good at damage).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3443_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3443\" data-vbnamecard=\"3443\">aluminiumtrioxid</a> etc have it right \u2013 with your default build you'll be a beast against most published things, and if you're fighting alongside other similar Solars you could slap down 'most anything in a straight fight. But you're Celestial Exalts, that's appropriate.<br /> <br /> Your ST will likely need to wear you out (multiple fight scenes against several opponents, poison, environmental penalties, that kinda thing) to trouble you. More ability/attribute dots pushes your ceilings higher, but unless you are fighting, like, multiple high essence Deebs every single fight you're more likely to notice that they give you more stamina \u2013 you won't need to burn as many motes to beat medium opposition across multiple scenes.<br /> <br /> The character you describe is dangerous, rest assured. Not min-max god-tier maybe, but deadly to published opponents. And he's interesting, which is the most important thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 09-16-2020, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:24:35-07:00","id":1414047,"title":"","content":"The grapple initiative roll is only difficulty 2 so with Vicious Lunge you pretty much can\u2019t fail it. The only time you should be rolling Dexterity to hit is when you\u2019re crashed and can\u2019t grapple at all.<br /> <br /> Unbreakable Grasp is essential, without it the Defense penalty while grappling basically means losing two rounds of control every time your opponent\u2019s turn comes up.<br /> <br /> Per the sidebar on page 257, don\u2019t forget to ask the ST how hard and far you can Nine Aeons Crashing Wave Throw someone and whether your powerlifting Charms substitute for Dragon Coil Technique if you want to suplex a train.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 09-16-2020, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:42:19-07:00","id":1414055,"title":"","content":"Based on a dev comment (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1182631#post1182631\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...31#post1182631</a>) Octavian should also be on the boostable to &gt;8 list. Even without that he has parry 7<br /> I'd also note that Fakharu's Flowing Body Dispersal, while not technically booting his defense, does functionally boost his defense by an average of 1 per 5 dice rolled, arguable putting him in the 8+ range, at least against any attack capable of hitting him at all.<br /> Alveua should be bold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:53:34-07:00","id":1414061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1414031#post1414031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's sort of why I'm asking. I want to be able to wrestle an Earth Immaculate, with at least a good chance of success.</div> </div> </div> </div>With 3 Dex, 5 Brawl and a specialty you will roll an immaculate of Earth. If you have only 7i, which you can easily start with, and you try for a grapple gambit right off the hop using Vicious Lunge, you will succeed on that initiative roll 95% of the time. Then you with a full excellency have 21 dice compared to their full excellency of 13. For a direct comparison here's what you're looking at, I'll put your stats in the first column and his in the second. Bolded are full excellency versions<br /> <br /> Withering Attack:<br /> 13&gt;12<br /> <b>21&gt;18</b><br /> <br /> Decisive Attack:<br /> 9&lt;12<br /> <b>17&lt;18</b><br /> <br /> Defense:<br /> 5&lt;6<br /> <b>9=9</b><br /> <br /> Control Roll:<br /> 11&gt;9<br /> <b>21&gt;13</b><br /> <br /> So as long as you're spending motes, you either match or beat him in every catagory, except decisive attack where you only miss out by 1. So with only the excellency and no other charms, you're beating an exalted martial artist at grappling. For anyone less than an exalt, like for example a gigantic demonic gorilla with arms like oak trees, you will make them cry.<br /> <br /> When you start getting<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1414031#post1414031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the expectation is that I'm supposed to be throwing out 8-10 motes on every attack, and then again on my control roll (and maybe to get my parry higher than 5, so I can be in bold on your list) that changes things significantly. But I'm under the impression that I'll need a round or two of withering attacks to be able to land that decisive grapple Gambit. And I'll be losing either motes or initiative (or both) every time I get attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're throwing 8-10 motes onto an attack, unless you're facing a powerful Deathknight or something, you're simply going to hit. There's a 1 in 100 chance that maybe you don't, but basically, you hit. If you're throwing 8-10 motes onto your defense unless, again, you're facing someone like a Dragonblooded Great House Matriarch, you won't be hit. Bloodapes are very deadly demons, they have 11 dice to their best attack, 9 dice to their bone-shattering roar. God-dogs the size of tigers with teeth that shatter steel have 10 dice to their best attack. An enormous predatory fish the size of a whale, with scales like steel armor and jaws that snap open so quickly they create whirlpools have 10 dice to their best attack.<br /> <br /> Basically the only way you're getting hit if you have Dex 3, Brawl 5 and a specialty is if you get ganged up on by a whole pack of Claw Striders or something. Which can happen, but hopefully your character isn't going solo everywhere that a half dozen dinosaur-monsters are likely to be hunting.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're in a place where you can't flare your anima banner, or when you're trying to conserve motes, you might get hit, but that's okay. This isn't 2e where getting touched by anything instantly kills you. Most things won't ever get the chance to even attempt a decisive attack against you, as the PCs generally beat them in initiative and crash them before they get to go. The only way you're really going to be taking decisive damage is if you're outnumbered and can't crash every enemy before they go, and then one of them launches a weak starting decisive, which might deal like 1-2 damage to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:56:40-07:00","id":1414063,"title":"","content":"Looking over some of the stats, I realized that without charms, I've basically built a blood ape. I'm ... surprisingly ok with that. That's probably strong enough for combat purposes, and it's mostly with Athletics charms that he'll do all his out of combat strong schtick. Is hitting someone with a pillar or a wagon or a thrown yeddim still under brawl? I understand that improvised weapons will cost me 1 init per use, just want to make sure I can do cool things with that strength, besides that grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:58:00-07:00","id":1414064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1414061#post1414061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't 2e where getting touched by anything instantly kills you. Most things won't ever get the chance to even attempt a decisive attack against you, as the PCs generally beat them in initiative and crash them before they get to go. The only way you're really going to be taking decisive damage is if you're outnumbered and can't crash every enemy before they go, and then one of them launches a weak starting decisive, which might deal like 1-2 damage to you.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that's what I needed to hear. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T15:04:55-07:00","id":1414067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1414055#post1414055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on a dev comment (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1182631#post1182631\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...31#post1182631</a>) Octavian should also be on the boostable to &gt;8 list. Even without that he has parry 7<br /> I'd also note that Fakharu's Flowing Body Dispersal, while not technically booting his defense, does functionally boost his defense by an average of 1 per 5 dice rolled, arguable putting him in the 8+ range, at least against any attack capable of hitting him at all.<br /> Alveua should be bold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I missed those.<br /> <br /> Still that's 25% of enemies who are in the &quot;At worst you hit 9/10 times&quot; range, and less than 10% in the &quot;At worst you miss 2 out of 5 times&quot; range. Again, not counting things like wound or onslaught penalties, which only some Exalted have the powers to cancel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T15:09:14-07:00","id":1414069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1414063#post1414063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking over some of the stats, I realized that without charms, I've basically built a blood ape. I'm ... surprisingly ok with that. That's probably strong enough for combat purposes, and it's mostly with Athletics charms that he'll do all his out of combat strong schtick. Is hitting someone with a pillar or a wagon or a thrown yeddim still under brawl? I understand that improvised weapons will cost me 1 init per use, just want to make sure I can do cool things with that strength, besides that grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodapes are also some of the most powerful creatures out there. Most things in Creation can't fight a bloodape, and you can match one with your mortal statline before even spending motes. I'd say pretty good.<br /> <br /> Also yes hitting somebody with a wagon is still under Brawl, although depending on what you're trying to do that may be more of a custom gambit. like if you're trying to trap them under an upturned wagon or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T00:03:38-07:00","id":1414143,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26421_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26421\" data-vbnamecard=\"26421\">Scrollreader</a> I've played almost this exact character in 2e and a different Night in 3e, and I have to say this: its far easier to make Stealth outstrip Awareness than vice versa. Almost no one invests in Awareness enough to catch someone who invests in Stealth. And having been ST for someone who dipped Grapple Brawl, the second you get your hands on someone they are dead and the ST is just rp'ing their turns for the sake of decency. Grapple Brawl is opposed by Grapple Brawl, unlike basically everything else. <br /> <br /> Combining Stealth with Grappling means that literally you will never be in danger from anyone not specifically specc'd to kill you. At Chargen you can make this character into juiced up Bane cosplaying as Ninja Batman and nobody can stop you unless they ambush you at noon in an empty field (or are Snipers). <br /> <br /> Don't worry about the limbo game of lowering your dex, this build is virtually unopposable in normal play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T01:06:24-07:00","id":1414153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380422-character-building-optimization-and-deoptimization-thread?p=1413975#post1413975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was wondering if I could get some help tuning a potential PC. I want to play a str focused supernatural Ath night caste. As such, he's looking at Str 5 and Mighty Thews 3 to start, along with Giant (doesn't actually make him stronger, but fits the Concept and might let him explain away some charms). He's probably looking at grapple brawl. Is Brawl 5 with dex 3 going to be basically fine, or will it mean he's trivializing combat encounters? Besides Brawl, he's probably looking at Ath 5 (Strength). Assume he wants to be able to beat up some dudes, maybe a DB or wrestle something suitability beefy. I'm not trying to make Invincible Punch Dude, here (or I'd be playing a Brawl Dawn), but it's important that his Str is basically Unmatched. And actually getting to hit or grab people is kind of important to making him more than just 'the guy who whiffs all the time'. Also, I'm debating where to put his Stamina. Another 5 is affordable, and fits the mental image, as well as making Resistance charms work better. Tentatively, he's probably taking Iron Skin Concentration, 1 Ox-Body, Vicious Lunge, Devil Strangling Attitude, and Armor Eating Strike. Too many combat charms? 3 defensive, 3 offensive, and a Ox-Body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fine.<br /> <br /> I posted my advice for creating combat capable characters <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1375559#post1375559\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> This character is on the boarder between &quot;Combat Capable Exalted Hero&quot; and &quot;Unstoppable God of War&quot;. It's not going to outshine a dedicated Dawn, but far outshines the &quot;properly terrifying Exalted assassin&quot; the Corebook presents us with. It looks great, I'd happily ST for this character.<br /> <br /> I don't think Stamina 5 is required, but it sounds like it fits the concept if that's what you're into. (Like Giant, it seems like it's a good narrative fit but not essential to the character concept.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Most of my previous experience is in prior editions, so I am under the impression that soak and resistance are generally worse than not getting hit, and that dex is the combat stat that really makes a difference. Please let me know if these assumptions need to be updated. </div> </div> </div>Eh... kinda?<br /> <br /> Dexterity is still the god-stat, but Vicious Lunge helps with that. Soak and resistance are much, much, much more useful than in 2E (much, much more useful than 2.5)... but it's <i>usually </i>still better to just not get hit.<br /> <br /> Because of the way mote regeneration and withering attacks work, it's often a good idea to blow motes on attacking and just allow yourself to get hit by withering attacks to save motes. But that's a <i>very </i>general rule of thumb, with lots of exceptions.<br /> <br /> My only salient advice here, is how are the other characters built?<br /> <br /> Because if everyone has mercilessly optimized for combat, you are going to be left in the dust. You've got the bones for an excellent character here, but the Exalted can be much stronger than this if you min-max.<br /> <br /> Whereas if everyone has kinda shrugged their shoulders at combat and taken, like, Melee 2 with one charm, you're going to be way overspecced. (And if anyone is really bad at designing Exalted characters and just picked up a pre-gen from Tomb of Dreams, or copy-pasted from the example in the Corebook, you are going to absolutely dominate.) The Exalted can be much weaker than this and still be fun, interesting characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}